course: dictionary
lesson: 1737
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word clan is a good example. Read the whole sentence first, then ask which meaning fits.
explain: «Spotted hyenas live in clans led by females.» Here a clan is a group of animals that live together. In Scotland and Ireland, a clan is a large group of families who share the same ancestor, so the word can mean a family group too.
explain: «The whole clan came for Christmas.» This is informal, so clan means a big, close family. Online, a clan can also be a team of players in a game. Test each meaning in the sentence and keep the one that makes sense.
fact: A clan is a large group of families who share the same ancestor, especially in Scotland and Ireland.
fact: Informally, a clan is a big, close family or a group of friends who stick together.
fact: In online games, a clan is a team of players.
fact: A spotted hyena clan can have up to about 80 members, and its females are in charge.
fact: A word can have several meanings, so always check which one fits the sentence.
exercise: «Spotted hyenas live in clans led by females.» In this sentence, what is a clan? | *A group of animals that live together | A wild storm at sea | A hot drink | A kind of cloth with stripes
exercise: Kai says, «My clan won the match last night.» What does clan mean here? | *A team of players in an online game | A big family in Scotland | A group of hyenas | A type of trophy
exercise: The MacDonalds were a Scottish clan with chiefs and tartans. What is a clan, in the Scottish sense? | A kind of tartan cloth | A chief who rules alone | A Scottish castle on a hill | *A large group of families who share the same ancestor
test: «In spotted hyena clans the females are in charge.» Clan here means: | A loud noise at night | A type of hyena food | *A group of animals that live together | A game of chance
test: Ella says, «Our clan is always there for each other.» What does clan mean? | A team in an online game | A tartan pattern | *A big, close family or group of friends | A sort of fishing net
exam: «Clan mothers chose chiefs and could remove them.» In this sentence, what does clan mean? | A kind of chief | A dance performed at festivals | *A group of families who share the same ancestor | A river in North America
